 "final_message": "All 12 work items are done, and the tests pass (6 in total, including the two new ones). I only ran the existing suite plus the two tests I added. I didn't add tests for the other fixes.\n\n**Items 1\u20138:** `conversion_rate`, `pooled_conversion_rate`, `conversions_in_window`, `parse_session_log`, `dedupe_sessions`, `daily_conversion_counts` and `campaign_summary` now follow SPEC sections 1\u20137. `parse_session_log` also raises `ValueError` for a `converted` value other than `1`, `0` or empty. The spec doesn't say what to do with those values, so that was my choice.\n\n**Items 9\u201310:** I added a test for the `None` rule in section 1 and one for keeping the last duplicate id in section 5. Both are in `tests/test_metrics.py`.\n\n**Item 11:** In the README, `conversions_in_window` now says it sums the last `days` entries. `daily_conversion_counts` has a new entry.\n\n**Item 12:** Checking the rest of the package against SPEC turned up three more bugs:\n- **`top_converting_groups`:** it now excludes empty groups and breaks ties by group name. It also no longer slices with a negative `n`.\n- **`conversion_rate_by_group`:** empty groups now map to `None`, and the keys are sorted.\n- **`longest_positive_streak`:** it never reset the run length after a zero, so it overcounted. It now resets.\n\nThe directory isn't a git repository, so I didn't make a commit.",
